    "description": {
      "value": "<p data-start=\"3566\" data-end=\"3639\">Once per Soma Break, when you remove or negate something, you may declare:</p><p data-start=\"3641\" data-end=\"3661\"><strong data-start=\"3641\" data-end=\"3661\">Total Redaction.</strong></p><p data-start=\"3663\" data-end=\"3676\">Within scope:</p><ul data-start=\"3678\" data-end=\"3820\"><li data-start=\"3678\" data-end=\"3736\"><p data-start=\"3680\" data-end=\"3736\">Summons cannot be re-summoned by that source for a time.</p></li><li data-start=\"3737\" data-end=\"3762\"><p data-start=\"3739\" data-end=\"3762\">Curses cannot reattach.</p></li><li data-start=\"3763\" data-end=\"3787\"><p data-start=\"3765\" data-end=\"3787\">Teleport anchors fail.</p></li><li data-start=\"3788\" data-end=\"3820\"><p data-start=\"3790\" data-end=\"3820\">Reanimation attempts collapse.</p></li></ul><p data-start=\"3822\" data-end=\"3840\">This does <strong data-start=\"3832\" data-end=\"3839\">not</strong>:</p><ul data-start=\"3842\" data-end=\"3900\"><li data-start=\"3842\" data-end=\"3856\"><p data-start=\"3844\" data-end=\"3856\">Erase canon.</p></li><li data-start=\"3857\" data-end=\"3874\"><p data-start=\"3859\" data-end=\"3874\">Kill immortals.</p></li><li data-start=\"3875\" data-end=\"3900\"><p data-start=\"3877\" data-end=\"3900\">Undo narrative Lore.</p></li></ul><p data-start=\"3902\" data-end=\"3948\">It enforces finality within your jurisdiction.</p><p data-start=\"3950\" data-end=\"3986\">Major misfire risk.<br data-start=\"3963\" data-end=\"3966\" />Backlash guaranteed.</p><p data-start=\"3988\" data-end=\"4020\">Redactors don\u2019t erase existence.</p><p data-start=\"4022\" data-end=\"4045\">They erase permissions.</p><p><em>Recosted 2026-08-23: this ability's earlier economy (Civic Charge / Strain / Resonance / Leverage / Administrative Pressure) is retired \u2014 everything now runs on Surge, Clarity, Noise, and the misfire ladder. The ability dialog's cost line is the truth; ledgers named here are narrative, GM-adjudicated, never a tracked pool.</em></p>",
